Yeah, it's for our catering business.

7
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:27,980
Oh.

8
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:27,980
I think I know that girl.

9
00:00:30,110 --> 00:00:33,690
We're not gonna keep it this way, though.

10
00:00:30,110 --> 00:00:33,690
No?

11
00:00:33,860 --> 00:00:36,910
We're gonna paint over the sword and replace it with a baguette.

12
00:00:37,070 --> 00:00:38,740
Oh.

13
00:00:38,910 --> 00:00:42,160
Um, also, we don't know what to do with this.

14
00:00:44,960 --> 00:00:47,210
Oh, yeah, I definitely know her.

15
00:01:38,050 --> 00:01:41,300
Remember that guy from cooking school that put cilantro in everything?

16
00:01:41,470 --> 00:01:43,310
Oh, sure, Cilantro Larry.

17
00:01:41,470 --> 00:01:43,310
Yeah.

18
00:01:44,140 --> 00:01:47,600
Well, I'm gonna fill in for him as food critic for the Chelsea Reporter.

19
00:01:47,770 --> 00:01:52,610
Wow. Monica, what an amazing opportunity to influence...

20
00:01:52,770 --> 00:01:54,320
...dozens of people.

21
00:01:56,950 --> 00:01:59,150
What about our catering business?

22
00:01:59,320 --> 00:02:01,160
Oh, no, no, it's just one night a week.

23
00:02:01,320 --> 00:02:03,950
Plus, I get to take all of you out for free dinners.

24
00:02:04,120 --> 00:02:05,290
Hey.

25
00:02:04,120 --> 00:02:05,290
Oh.

26
00:02:05,450 --> 00:02:06,540
Well, in that case:

27
00:02:10,670 --> 00:02:13,000
That was me hopping onboard.

28
00:02:10,670 --> 00:02:13,000
Oh.

29
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:18,010
Hey, guys. Hey, Ross. Quick question for you.

30
00:02:18,170 --> 00:02:19,680
Are you ready to party?

31
00:02:20,930 --> 00:02:23,550
I don't know, I could maybe go out for a couple of beers.

32
00:02:23,720 --> 00:02:27,850
But there's this thing about bumblebees on the Discovery Channel.

33
00:02:28,940 --> 00:02:33,230
No, no, no, I don't think you heard me. Are you ready to party?

34
00:02:34,730 --> 00:02:36,530
No.

35
00:02:36,690 --> 00:02:38,860
Gandalf? Gandalf is coming to town?

36
00:02:39,030 --> 00:02:41,160
Kathy's with her parents, I have nothing to do.

37
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:43,700
Tomorrow we are partying with Gandalf, dude.

38
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:48,620
Dude, we are so gonna party. Yeah.

39
00:02:48,790 --> 00:02:50,660
Wow, okay. Dude alert.

40
00:02:52,830 --> 00:02:54,170
And who is this guy?

41
00:02:54,340 --> 00:02:58,590
Mike "Gandalf" Ganderson. Only, like, the funnest guy in the world.

42
00:02:58,760 --> 00:03:00,380
I'm gonna call and get off work tomorrow.

43
00:03:00,550 --> 00:03:03,720
Oh. I'm gonna call after you.

44
00:03:03,890 --> 00:03:06,850
This is gonna be so cool. Dude, we never party anymore.

45
00:03:07,020 --> 00:03:09,270
Whoo!

46
00:03:09,770 --> 00:03:13,270
All right, were you guys smoking something in the back of our van?

47
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:17,610
What do you mean, we never have fun? You have fun with me.

48
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:21,900
Remember the time we saw those strippers and you paid me 50 bucks to eat that book?

49
00:03:23,530 --> 00:03:28,200
Joey, you are gonna love this guy. Gandalf is like the party wizard.

50
00:03:28,370 --> 00:03:32,000
Well, why do you call him Gandalf?

51
00:03:28,370 --> 00:03:32,000
Gandalf the wizard.

52
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:36,710
Hello? Didn't you read Lord of the Rings in high school?

53
00:03:38,340 --> 00:03:39,760
No, I had sex in high school.

54
00:03:46,430 --> 00:03:50,520
Oh. Uh, Joanna? I was wondering if I could ask you something.

55
00:03:50,680 --> 00:03:53,390
There's an opening for an assistant buyer in Junior Miss...

56
00:03:53,560 --> 00:03:55,600
Okay, but that would be a step down for me.

57
00:03:55,770 --> 00:03:58,230
No, actually, I meant for me.

58
00:03:58,820 --> 00:04:00,940
The hiring committee is meeting people all day and...

59
00:04:01,110 --> 00:04:06,110
Oh. Well, I wish I could say no, but I guess you can't stay my assistant forever.

60
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:09,200
Neither can you, Sophie, but for different reasons.

61
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:13,120
I'm so glad you don't have a problem with this.

62
00:04:13,290 --> 00:04:15,620
If you did, I wouldn't have considered applying.

63
00:04:15,790 --> 00:04:16,830
Really? In that case...

64
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:19,210
And that's why I'm so glad there's no problem.

65
00:04:19,840 --> 00:04:23,840
Yeah, it's fine. I'm on the hiring committee, so there'll be one friendly face.

66
00:04:24,010 --> 00:04:25,430
Oh, that's great.

67
00:04:25,590 --> 00:04:28,180
You know, Junior Miss is where I started.

68
00:04:25,590 --> 00:04:28,180
Really?

69
00:04:28,350 --> 00:04:31,600
I had to sleep with the ugliest guy to get that job.

70
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:36,230
Really?

71
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:36,230
No. Ha, ha.

72
00:04:36,400 --> 00:04:37,980
Yeah.

73
00:04:38,980 --> 00:04:41,690
I mean, no. No, no, no. Ha, ha.

74
00:04:38,980 --> 00:04:41,690
No. Ha, ha.

75
00:04:41,860 --> 00:04:45,200
I'm sure with your qualifications, you won't need to sleep with some guy.

76
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:46,410
Oh. Ha, ha.

77
00:04:46,570 --> 00:04:48,700
Although, uh, I might need some convincing.

78
00:04:50,870 --> 00:04:52,910
Um... Oh.

79
00:04:50,870 --> 00:04:52,910
Kidding. Ha, ha.

80
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:57,250
God, I feel wild today.

81
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:57,250
Aah!

82
00:05:02,340 --> 00:05:05,670
Oh, man, I am so excited, I may vomit.

83
00:05:07,010 --> 00:05:10,600
Will you calm down? He's just a human guy.

84
00:05:11,100 --> 00:05:13,560
Look, you don't understand. Gandalf is amazing.

85
00:05:13,730 --> 00:05:15,350
You never know what's gonna happen.

86
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:19,980
You go out for a couple of beers and end up on a fishing boat to Nova Scotia.

87
00:05:20,150 --> 00:05:22,770
Really?

88
00:05:20,150 --> 00:05:22,770
Oh, yeah, it's beautiful country up there.

89
00:05:23,570 --> 00:05:25,190
Hey. Okay.

90
00:05:25,360 --> 00:05:30,200
I got my passport, fresh socks, and a snakebite kit.

91
00:05:30,910 --> 00:05:33,040
It's not gonna be exactly like last time.

92
00:05:34,870 --> 00:05:36,040
All right, I'll see you guys.

93
00:05:36,210 --> 00:05:38,830
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

94
00:05:39,460 --> 00:05:41,880
I have an audition, but I'll hook up with you later.

95
00:05:42,050 --> 00:05:43,880
Where you gonna be around noon?

96
00:05:42,050 --> 00:05:43,880
Heh.

97
00:05:44,050 --> 00:05:46,170
Somewhere maybe along the equator?

98
00:05:48,430 --> 00:05:49,840
Okay.

99
00:05:52,350 --> 00:05:53,640
Hello?

100
00:05:53,810 --> 00:05:54,970
It's Gandalf.

101
00:05:57,890 --> 00:05:59,770
So are you in town?

102
00:06:01,900 --> 00:06:03,440
Oh, well...

103
00:06:04,030 --> 00:06:06,070
Well, maybe next time, then.

104
00:06:06,940 --> 00:06:08,030
What happened?

105
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:10,280
He's not gonna make it. He's stuck in Chicago.

106
00:06:10,450 --> 00:06:11,780
Oh, man.

107
00:06:11,950 --> 00:06:14,620
Chicago's so lucky.

108
00:06:15,330 --> 00:06:19,290
Stupid, useless Canadian money.

109
00:06:24,840 --> 00:06:27,800
You have a very impressive résumé, Ms. Green.

110
00:06:27,970 --> 00:06:32,300
I especially like what I see here about implementing a new filing system.

111
00:06:32,470 --> 00:06:33,970
Thank you.

112
00:06:34,140 --> 00:06:38,100
Filing system? Oh, you mean those little colored labels you put on all the folders?

113
00:06:38,270 --> 00:06:41,650
It certainly did brighten up the inside of the filing cabinets.

114
00:06:42,480 --> 00:06:46,270
Well, they, uh... They did more than that.

115
00:06:46,440 --> 00:06:50,490
I notice that you've been entrusted with a lot of important responsibilities.

116
00:06:50,660 --> 00:06:55,160
Yes. Joanna really has been an incredible mentor to me.

117
00:06:55,330 --> 00:06:59,120
Oh. And Rachel has been really incredible at getting my morning bagel.

118
00:06:59,290 --> 00:07:01,920
It's amazing how she gets it right almost every time.

119
00:07:03,420 --> 00:07:06,380
Of course, I have more responsibilities than that.

120
00:07:06,550 --> 00:07:12,130
Oh, yes, of course. There's the coffee too. Rachel can carry two things at once.

121
00:07:13,180 --> 00:07:15,640
That's, uh, very good.

122
00:07:16,310 --> 00:07:18,850
Now, a big part of this job...

123
00:07:19,020 --> 00:07:22,940
...is cultivating personal relationships, especially with designers.

124
00:07:23,100 --> 00:07:25,650
Yes, I realize...

125
00:07:23,100 --> 00:07:25,650
Rachel shouldn't have any problem.

126
00:07:25,820 --> 00:07:29,530
Her only problem might be getting a little too friendly, if you know what I mean.

127
00:07:30,650 --> 00:07:32,400
I love working with designers.

128
00:07:32,570 --> 00:07:35,700
With them, under them, what's the difference, eh, Rach?

129
00:07:41,620 --> 00:07:43,620
Hey. My first review is out.

130
00:07:43,790 --> 00:07:46,540
Oh! Oh, the Chelsea Reporter.

131
00:07:46,710 --> 00:07:50,010
Ah. These used to keep me so warm.

132
00:07:50,670 --> 00:07:53,050
All right, look, I'm on the back page.

133
00:07:50,670 --> 00:07:53,050
Ooh. Oh!

134
00:07:53,220 --> 00:07:57,430
Okay. "Would I go back to Allesandro's? Sure, but I would have to order two meals.

135
00:07:57,600 --> 00:08:01,180
One for me, and one for the guy pointing the gun to my head."

136
00:08:01,890 --> 00:08:04,310
Wow, you really laid into this place.

137
00:08:04,480 --> 00:08:07,650
Hey, they don't pay me a penny a word to make friends.

138
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:11,320
Ooh, I gotta go. I found a guy who could fix up the van for catering.

139
00:08:11,490 --> 00:08:13,700
Oh. You want me to go with you?

140
00:08:11,490 --> 00:08:13,700
No, no, it's okay.

141
00:08:13,860 --> 00:08:16,570
But are we sure we don't want the waterbed?

142
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:20,290
Haven't we made this decision?

143
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:20,290
Yeah, all right.

144
00:08:22,080 --> 00:08:23,540
Bye.

145
00:08:22,080 --> 00:08:23,540
Bye.

146
00:08:29,840 --> 00:08:30,880
Who is it?

147
00:08:31,050 --> 00:08:33,840
It's Allesandro, from Allesandro's.

148
00:08:35,470 --> 00:08:36,510
Oh, my God.

149
00:08:36,680 --> 00:08:39,930
I wanna talk to you about your review.

150
00:08:36,680 --> 00:08:39,930
Oh, my God. Oh, my God.

151
00:08:40,100 --> 00:08:42,310
Call me on the phone.

152
00:08:42,930 --> 00:08:45,350
What, so you can hang up on me?

153
00:08:45,520 --> 00:08:48,270
I'm never gonna let you up, so you may as well just go away.

154
00:08:48,440 --> 00:08:49,650
Just give me a chance to...

155
00:08:49,820 --> 00:08:52,110
Do you need to get in? Here you go.

156
00:08:52,280 --> 00:08:54,320
No, Phoebe!

157
00:08:52,280 --> 00:08:54,320
Oh, hey, Monica.

158
00:09:00,660 --> 00:09:04,540
I want a retraction. Our food is not "inedible swill."

159
00:09:04,710 --> 00:09:05,750
I couldn't eat it.

160
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:09,420
I have five friends who couldn't eat it, and one of them eats books.

161
00:09:10,750 --> 00:09:13,000
Well, our service is not "grossly incompetent."

162
00:09:13,170 --> 00:09:16,300
The waiter carried the breadsticks in his pants.

163
00:09:17,550 --> 00:09:21,350
Well, you said that we accept the Discover Card...

164
00:09:21,510 --> 00:09:23,930
...which we do not.

165
00:09:24,390 --> 00:09:26,810
All right, that I'll retract.

166
00:09:26,980 --> 00:09:30,190
But I stand by my review. I know food, and that wasn't it.

167
00:09:30,650 --> 00:09:32,730
Your marinara sauce tastes like tomato juice.

168
00:09:32,900 --> 00:09:35,860
You should serve it with vodka and a piece of celery.

169
00:09:36,030 --> 00:09:38,360
Hey, I'm proud of that sauce. It's delicious.

170
00:09:38,530 --> 00:09:39,950
Oh, my God.

171
00:09:40,120 --> 00:09:42,910
You own an Italian restaurant and you think that tastes good?

172
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:44,200
Where are you even from?

173
00:09:45,910 --> 00:09:47,750
Lebanon.

174
00:09:49,130 --> 00:09:50,170
Hand me those tomatoes.

175
00:09:50,330 --> 00:09:53,840
I'm gonna show you what it should taste like. Come on, hand them to me.

176
00:09:55,010 --> 00:09:58,510
How long is this gonna take? I got another critic I gotta go yell at.

177
00:10:04,850 --> 00:10:07,810
Ahem. Uh, Joanna, I wanna talk about that interview.

178
00:10:07,980 --> 00:10:10,230
I thought it went very well.

179
00:10:11,060 --> 00:10:15,860
No, it didn't. That's what I wanna talk to you about.

180
00:10:16,780 --> 00:10:18,990
[IN STRAINED VOICE] Now, just to brief you...

181
00:10:20,700 --> 00:10:22,700
...I may cry.

182
00:10:23,700 --> 00:10:27,620
But they are not tears of sadness or of anger...

183
00:10:27,790 --> 00:10:30,250
...but just of me having this discussion with you.

184
00:10:31,210 --> 00:10:33,130
Rachel, please, don't make a scene.

185
00:10:33,790 --> 00:10:35,920
There's nobody here.

186
00:10:36,090 --> 00:10:37,920
Sophie, get in here.

187
00:10:40,010 --> 00:10:42,890
You see? Now you're making Sophie uncomfortable.

188
00:10:43,050 --> 00:10:44,760
She's not making me uncomfortable.

189
00:10:44,930 --> 00:10:49,020
Congratulations, you've just crossed the line into completely useless. Get out.

190
00:10:51,770 --> 00:10:53,400
[IN NORMAL VOICE] Do you want me to quit?

191
00:10:53,560 --> 00:10:55,650
What? What would make you think that?

192
00:10:56,730 --> 00:10:59,150
Well, all of those things you said in the interview.

193
00:10:59,320 --> 00:11:02,450
If you believe any of them, I must not be a very good assistant.

194
00:11:04,450 --> 00:11:05,660
You know what?

195
00:11:06,160 --> 00:11:09,580
I am just going to pack up my desk...

196
00:11:10,870 --> 00:11:14,500
...and I will be gone by the end of the day.

197
00:11:17,960 --> 00:11:21,680
Well, I guess there's no use me sticking around till the end of the day.

198
00:11:22,390 --> 00:11:23,800
Wait, wait, wait.

199
00:11:23,970 --> 00:11:26,760
You can put your sad little muffin back in its drawer.

200
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:32,140
If you must know the truth, I didn't wanna lose a good assistant.

201
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:33,520
What?

202
00:11:33,690 --> 00:11:38,360
That's why I said all those things about your flirting and your drinking.

203
00:11:38,940 --> 00:11:40,190
My drinking?

204
00:11:41,610 --> 00:11:44,240
Oh. I must have said that after you left.

205
00:11:45,570 --> 00:11:46,950
Said what, exactly?

206
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:48,910
That you enjoy the occasional drink...

207
00:11:49,080 --> 00:11:50,910
ing binge.

208
00:11:52,210 --> 00:11:54,790
Oh, my God. Oh. That is it. I'm leaving.

209
00:11:54,960 --> 00:11:58,290
You are just a horrible person.

210
00:11:54,960 --> 00:11:58,290
No, wait, wait, wait.

211
00:11:58,460 --> 00:12:01,380
Now, if you're gonna get all sensitive about it.

212
00:12:01,550 --> 00:12:02,920
I don't want to lose you.

213
00:12:03,090 --> 00:12:05,640
What if I create a position for you?

214
00:12:05,800 --> 00:12:08,810
I'll make you assistant buyer in this department.

215
00:12:10,220 --> 00:12:12,730
Say more things like that.

216
00:12:10,220 --> 00:12:12,730
Um...

217
00:12:13,520 --> 00:12:16,520
You can have your own office and a raise, effective tomorrow.

218
00:12:17,310 --> 00:12:19,900
I'd need an expense account.

219
00:12:17,310 --> 00:12:19,900
Done.

220
00:12:20,440 --> 00:12:22,990
And an assistant.

221
00:12:20,440 --> 00:12:22,990
Sophie, get in here.

222
00:12:25,320 --> 00:12:29,240
Now it seems like a lifetime, doesn't it? Starting from...

223
00:12:29,410 --> 00:12:30,990
Hey, what are you guys doing here?

224
00:12:31,160 --> 00:12:34,830
I thought you'd be partying with Gandoldorf.

225
00:12:35,540 --> 00:12:38,670
It's Gandalf, and he's not coming.

226
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:42,170
So you've been sitting here all morning?

227
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:42,170
No.

228
00:12:42,340 --> 00:12:44,840
I balanced my checkbook.

229
00:12:45,430 --> 00:12:48,720
Yeah, and I gave first names to all the foosball players.

230
00:12:50,510 --> 00:12:53,020
I can't believe he didn't come.

231
00:12:53,180 --> 00:12:56,480
So what if he didn't come? We can still go out and party ourselves.

232
00:12:56,650 --> 00:13:00,320
Oh, no, you know, with Gandalf, we'd be out all night.

233
00:13:00,480 --> 00:13:04,740
Yeah, we'd meet total strangers and hang out with them.

234
00:13:04,900 --> 00:13:06,360
Well, we could do that.

235
00:13:07,740 --> 00:13:10,280
There was other stuff too.

236
00:13:10,950 --> 00:13:12,740
We'll do it all, and better.

237
00:13:12,910 --> 00:13:15,710
Look, after tonight, Gandalf will wanna party with us, dude.

238
00:13:15,870 --> 00:13:16,920
Come on.

239
00:13:17,500 --> 00:13:19,880
Yeah.

240
00:13:17,500 --> 00:13:19,880
Yeah.

241
00:13:20,040 --> 00:13:23,460
It's not like we don't know how to party.

242
00:13:20,040 --> 00:13:23,460
Yeah. All right. Let's go.

243
00:13:23,630 --> 00:13:25,590
And maybe we could end up on a boat again?

244
00:13:25,760 --> 00:13:27,220
Yeah!

245
00:13:25,760 --> 00:13:27,220
All right!

246
00:13:27,380 --> 00:13:28,590
Ah!

247
00:13:29,090 --> 00:13:32,140
Hey, hey, hey. When were we on a boat?

248
00:13:32,310 --> 00:13:34,100
Remember that really cold morning...

249
00:13:34,270 --> 00:13:36,940
...when you woke up and those dogs were licking your face?

250
00:13:37,100 --> 00:13:38,770
Yeah.

251
00:13:37,100 --> 00:13:38,770
Those were seals, man.

252
00:13:46,570 --> 00:13:49,660
Hey, how do you think this suit would look on an assistant buyer...?

253
00:13:49,820 --> 00:13:51,950
The owner of Allesandro's came to yell at me...

254
00:13:52,120 --> 00:13:55,330
...but I made him some sauce, and he offered me the job as head chef.

255
00:13:55,500 --> 00:13:56,540
Oh, my God.

256
00:13:56,710 --> 00:14:00,920
You just ruined the thing I was practicing the whole way home, but I'm so happy.

257
00:14:01,790 --> 00:14:04,380
Can you believe it? I finally get to run my own kitchen.

258
00:14:04,550 --> 00:14:05,590
Oh, you've waited so long.

259
00:14:07,970 --> 00:14:10,430
Hey.

260
00:14:07,970 --> 00:14:10,430
Hey, Pheebs. Quick question for you.

261
00:14:10,590 --> 00:14:14,970
How do you think this suit would look on an assistant buyer at Bloomingdale's?

262
00:14:15,140 --> 00:14:18,940
I don't know. It would totally depend on her coloring and...

263
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:20,980
You got the job!

264
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:20,980
Yes!

265
00:14:21,150 --> 00:14:24,020
Oh! You got the job? Why didn't you tell me?

266
00:14:26,650 --> 00:14:30,320
Oh. It's gonna be so great. I'm gonna get to help decide what we sell.

267
00:14:30,490 --> 00:14:33,160
I'm gonna have an office with walls and everything.

268
00:14:33,330 --> 00:14:36,290
I'm gonna have walls.

269
00:14:33,330 --> 00:14:36,290
Aw.

270
00:14:36,450 --> 00:14:39,790
Is this the day of good news or what? I got us a job.

271
00:14:39,960 --> 00:14:41,040
The wedding reception.

272
00:14:41,210 --> 00:14:42,670
Oh.

273
00:14:43,630 --> 00:14:47,130
Um, Phoebe, I kind of need to talk to you about that.

274
00:14:49,630 --> 00:14:50,800
Um...

275
00:14:51,550 --> 00:14:55,720
Well, I think it might be time for me to take a step back from the catering.

276
00:14:55,890 --> 00:14:58,640
But we've only had one job.

277
00:14:55,890 --> 00:14:58,640
Tsk.

278
00:14:58,810 --> 00:15:03,560
I know, but now we have this second one, and it just feels like it's snowballing.

279
00:15:04,860 --> 00:15:06,190
Yeah, what are you saying?

280
00:15:06,820 --> 00:15:09,690
I got offered the head-chef job at Allesandro's.

281
00:15:10,110 --> 00:15:14,370
What?

282
00:15:10,110 --> 00:15:14,370
It's okay, you don't really need me.

283
00:15:14,870 --> 00:15:16,910
You're the cook.

284
00:15:17,700 --> 00:15:20,370
Without you, it's just me driving up to people's houses...

285
00:15:20,540 --> 00:15:22,540
...with empty trays and asking for money.

286
00:15:26,500 --> 00:15:27,500
All right.

287
00:15:27,670 --> 00:15:31,090
But, um, well, I'll pay you back all the money you invested.

288
00:15:31,260 --> 00:15:34,390
And you can keep the van.

289
00:15:31,260 --> 00:15:34,390
For what?

290
00:15:36,010 --> 00:15:39,430
I can't believe this. I gotta get out of here.

291
00:15:39,600 --> 00:15:41,730
Phoebe, wait a minute.

292
00:15:44,980 --> 00:15:47,360
I'm an assistant buyer!

293
00:15:51,860 --> 00:15:55,410
All right, we'll get a little coffee, get energized, then we'll head back out.

294
00:15:55,570 --> 00:15:57,870
Yeah, all right.

295
00:15:55,570 --> 00:15:57,870
Okay.

296
00:16:01,040 --> 00:16:05,040
So we're having fun, right? We don't need that wizard guy.

297
00:16:05,210 --> 00:16:08,210
We hit a couple of clubs, talked to some strangers...

298
00:16:08,380 --> 00:16:11,920
...then after this, we'll go down to the docks and see about that boat thing.

299
00:16:13,930 --> 00:16:16,180
I'm kind of beat.

300
00:16:16,640 --> 00:16:18,220
Actually...

301
00:16:18,390 --> 00:16:19,890
...me too.

302
00:16:20,060 --> 00:16:21,060
Are you serious?

303
00:16:21,230 --> 00:16:22,270
Yeah.

304
00:16:22,430 --> 00:16:24,190
Thank God. I'm exhausted.

305
00:16:26,690 --> 00:16:27,940
So you guys want coffees?

306
00:16:28,110 --> 00:16:31,280
Yeah, but I don't wanna be up too late, so I'll have a decaf.

307
00:16:31,440 --> 00:16:33,240
Yeah, me too.

308
00:16:33,400 --> 00:16:36,820
Actually, could I get some hot water with a little lemon?

309
00:16:37,530 --> 00:16:42,660
I strained my voice screaming in there. Does it have to be so loud?

310
00:16:42,830 --> 00:16:45,920
Oh. I can't hear a word you're saying, my ears are ringing so bad.

311
00:16:46,080 --> 00:16:49,670
Huh. I was glad I brought that extra pair of socks, you know?

312
00:16:49,840 --> 00:16:50,920
I used them as mittens.

313
00:16:51,090 --> 00:16:53,010
I didn't wanna touch a thing in that last place.

314
00:16:53,170 --> 00:16:54,420
Oh.

315
00:16:58,390 --> 00:17:00,760
How sad are we?

316
00:17:00,930 --> 00:17:02,270
Yeah, I know.

317
00:17:03,350 --> 00:17:05,230
You know what? We're not sad.

318
00:17:05,390 --> 00:17:07,730
We're not sad, we're just not 21 anymore, you know?

319
00:17:07,900 --> 00:17:09,400
I'm 29 years old, damn it.

320
00:17:09,570 --> 00:17:12,110
I wanna sit in a comfortable chair, watch television...

321
00:17:12,280 --> 00:17:14,110
...and go to sleep at a reasonable hour.

322
00:17:15,610 --> 00:17:19,280
Yeah, and I like to hang out in a quiet place where I can talk to my friends.

323
00:17:19,450 --> 00:17:20,490
Yeah.

324
00:17:20,660 --> 00:17:25,500
And so what if I like to go home, throw on some Kenny G, and take a bath?

325
00:17:29,250 --> 00:17:30,790
We're 29. We're not women.

326
00:17:38,590 --> 00:17:41,680
Oh. There you are.

327
00:17:42,100 --> 00:17:44,930
Hey, I'm glad that you decided to hear me out.

328
00:17:45,100 --> 00:17:47,190
Okay, I'm hearing.

329
00:17:47,850 --> 00:17:50,020
I've been doing a lot of thinking. A lot.

330
00:17:50,480 --> 00:17:55,190
And, well, I came up with a whole bunch of businesses that you can do with your van.

331
00:17:55,360 --> 00:17:56,860
Okay, um...

332
00:17:57,400 --> 00:18:00,620
You could be a flower delivery person.

333
00:17:57,400 --> 00:18:00,620
What?

334
00:18:00,780 --> 00:18:02,910
Or a bakery delivery person.

335
00:18:04,290 --> 00:18:05,330
Pizza?

336
00:18:06,040 --> 00:18:07,910
Monica.

337
00:18:08,080 --> 00:18:10,830
All right, I got a whole bunch of stuff in this area...

338
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:13,710
...but I'm getting the feeling you don't wanna deliver.

339
00:18:15,090 --> 00:18:17,920
No.

340
00:18:15,090 --> 00:18:17,920
Okay.

341
00:18:20,390 --> 00:18:22,350
I'm guessing if you don't wanna deliver...

342
00:18:22,510 --> 00:18:25,600
...you probably don't wanna pick up stuff either.

343
00:18:25,770 --> 00:18:27,310
No.

344
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:32,810
You know what?

345
00:18:33,230 --> 00:18:36,360
Let's do the catering business.

346
00:18:33,230 --> 00:18:36,360
Really? Are you sure?

347
00:18:36,530 --> 00:18:40,320
Yeah. You know, I made a commitment to you.

348
00:18:40,490 --> 00:18:43,530
Know what? Lt'd be fun.

349
00:18:40,490 --> 00:18:43,530
Oh, it will be fun.

350
00:18:45,870 --> 00:18:48,910
Okay. Ooh, let's plan the wedding reception. Okay.

351
00:18:52,960 --> 00:18:54,170
Wow.

352
00:18:56,090 --> 00:18:58,420
You really wanted me to do something with this van.

353
00:19:03,140 --> 00:19:06,010
You know what? I want you to take the chefjob.

354
00:19:06,640 --> 00:19:09,020
Really?

355
00:19:06,640 --> 00:19:09,020
Yeah.

356
00:19:09,180 --> 00:19:11,310
That's what you really want.

357
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:13,730
Yeah, I don't wanna be the reason you're unhappy.

358
00:19:13,900 --> 00:19:15,190
That would make me unhappy.

359
00:19:15,360 --> 00:19:18,400
And I really don't wanna be the reason I'm unhappy.

360
00:19:19,490 --> 00:19:21,150
Thank you.

361
00:19:23,660 --> 00:19:27,080
Besides, it might be kind of fun to form the new A-Team.

362
00:19:36,170 --> 00:19:39,090
Oh, hi, Mrs. Lynch. Is Joanna in already?

363
00:19:39,260 --> 00:19:41,970
Oh, my goodness. You haven't heard.

364
00:19:42,130 --> 00:19:43,630
Heard what?

365
00:19:43,800 --> 00:19:46,970
Joanna passed away last night.

366
00:19:47,140 --> 00:19:49,810
Oh, my God. How?

367
00:19:49,980 --> 00:19:52,890
Well, she was leaving work, and she was hit by a cab.

368
00:19:53,060 --> 00:19:55,940
Oh, my God. Oh, I cannot believe it.

369
00:19:56,110 --> 00:19:59,360
I know.

370
00:19:56,110 --> 00:19:59,360
Oh, God.

371
00:19:59,530 --> 00:20:04,610
Oh, God.

372
00:20:05,370 --> 00:20:07,990
I didn't realize that you were so close.

373
00:20:08,160 --> 00:20:11,750
Yes. So close.

374
00:20:13,420 --> 00:20:19,500
Mrs. Lynch, I know that this is an emotional and difficult time for all of us.

375
00:20:19,670 --> 00:20:23,510
But by any chance, did Joanna send any paperwork your way...

376
00:20:23,680 --> 00:20:26,640
...before it happened?

377
00:20:26,800 --> 00:20:29,140
No, nothing.

378
00:20:29,310 --> 00:20:33,940
Imagine, if she'd just stepped off that curb a few seconds later...

379
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:39,070
Oh. Yes, yes, just a few seconds and she'd still be with us.

380
00:20:39,230 --> 00:20:41,650
Nothing about an assistant buyer?

381
00:20:42,190 --> 00:20:44,530
I'm sorry. I have to go.

382
00:20:46,990 --> 00:20:47,990
Good morning.

383
00:20:48,160 --> 00:20:51,120
Oh, Sophie, I guess you didn't hear about Joanna.

384
00:20:51,290 --> 00:20:52,790
I sure did.

385
00:20:58,790 --> 00:21:01,840
I'm so excited about having Monica come onboard with us.

386
00:21:02,010 --> 00:21:05,840
Although I do feel bad about having fired Chef Emilio.

387
00:21:06,010 --> 00:21:08,760
It is like losing a member of the family.

388
00:21:08,930 --> 00:21:13,100
Of course, that literally is the case for several of you.

389
00:21:14,690 --> 00:21:17,350
Tony, Carlos, Marie...

390
00:21:17,520 --> 00:21:21,570
...please tell your father how much we're going to miss him.

391
00:21:23,650 --> 00:21:27,410
Now, I know that Monica has a lot of great ideas for this place.

392
00:21:27,570 --> 00:21:30,490
Well, you all read the review. Ha, ha.

393
00:21:30,660 --> 00:21:32,990
So without much further ado...

394
00:21:33,160 --> 00:21:37,290
...I present to you our new head chef.

395
00:21:43,460 --> 00:21:48,220
Um, I just wanna say, uh, that with a pinch of excitement...

396
00:21:48,390 --> 00:21:51,720
...a dash of hard work, and a dollop of cooperation...

397
00:21:51,890 --> 00:21:53,850
...we can have the recipe...

398
00:21:58,310 --> 00:21:59,560
Are you going to kill me?

